  "excerpt": "A sudden, painful acne flare-up can derail your confidence and leave your skin feeling inflamed, raw, and tender. Whether you are dealing with persistent cystic breakouts, hormonal acne along the jawline, or stubborn con",
  "html": "<p>A sudden, painful acne flare-up can derail your confidence and leave your skin feeling inflamed, raw, and tender. Whether you are dealing with persistent cystic breakouts, hormonal acne along the jawline, or stubborn congestion that over-the-counter cleansers refuse to fix, severe acne requires more than surface-level skincare.</p>\n<p>If you are looking for advanced <strong>severe acne flare up treatment options in St. Simons Island</strong>, professional medical intervention can calm active inflammation, clear deep-seated congestion, and prevent long-term scarring.</p>\n<h2>Home Care vs. Professional Medical Treatment for Severe Acne</h2>\n<p>When a major breakout hits, it is tempting to try aggressive home remedies, harsh scrubs, or multiple spot treatments. However, understanding when home care is sufficient—and when it is time to seek expert medical care—is critical to protecting your skin barrier.</p>\n<h3>When Home Care Works</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Occasional Whiteheads or Blackheads:</strong> Minor, surface-level congestion often responds well to gentle over-the-counter salicylic acid or benzoyl peroxide.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Mild Post-Sunscreens Breakouts:</strong> Temporary congestion caused by heavy products can clear up with simple exfoliation and proper double-cleansing.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>When to Seek Professional Medical Care</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Deep, Painful Cystic Nodules:</strong> Blind, throbbing bumps beneath the skin should never be picked or squeezed, as this drives inflammation deeper and leads to severe scarring.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Persistent Hormonal Breakouts:</strong> Acne clustered around the lower face, chin, and neck that cycles with stress or hormone fluctuations usually indicates underlying systemic triggers.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Redness, Swelling, and Hyperpigmentation:</strong> Active flare-ups that leave lasting dark spots, red marks, or pitted scars require clinical-grade technologies to reset the skin.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Medical-Grade Acne Solutions at Imber Medical</h2>\n<p>At <strong>Imber Medical</strong> on St. Simons Island, led by Board-Certified Physician Dr. Laura Slack, we take a clinical, root-cause approach to skin health. We do not rely on one-size-fits-all fixes. Instead, we combine state-of-the-art energy devices, medical-grade skin resurfacing, and functional wellness to stop severe acne at its source.</p>\n<h3>1. Breakthrough Laser Therapy: AviClear™</h3>\n<p>AviClear™ is the first and only FDA-cleared energy device specifically designed to treat mild, moderate, and severe acne.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>How It Works:</strong> Using a 1726 nm wavelength, AviClear selectively targets and downregulates the sebaceous (oil) glands. By suppressing excessive oil production—the core driver of acne—it provides long-term clearance without prescription drugs or harsh chemical side effects.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Protocol:</strong> A simple series of three 30-minute treatment sessions can deliver up to 90% clearance of cystic acne.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>2. Clinical Exfoliation &amp; Deep Pore Purification</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Acne-Clarifying HydraFacial®:</strong> Utilizing vortex-fusion technology, HydraFacial painlessly suctions out deep pore impurities, dead skin cells, and excess sebum while infusing the skin with hydration and calming salicylic boosters.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>VI Peel Medical Chemical Peels:</strong> For active breakouts combined with stubborn hyperpigmentation, the VI Peel purifies clogged pores, reduces active inflammation, and rapidly sheds discolored, dead skin layers.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>3. Advanced Scarring &amp; Post-Acne Texture Repair</h3>\n<p>Once the active flare-up is controlled, repairing post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation and pitted scars is the next step toward smooth skin.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Opus Plasma® Skin Resurfacing:</strong> Combining radiofrequency energy and fractional plasma, Opus Plasma repairs rough texture and stimulates deep collagen remodeling with minimal downtime.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Pico Genesis Laser:</strong> Uses nonthermal laser energy to shatter stubborn dark spots and acne scar discoloration, restoring an even tone.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>4. Functional Medicine: Healing Acne From the Inside Out</h3>\n<p>Acne is frequently an external symptom of an internal imbalance. Through <strong>Functional Medicine</strong> diagnostics, Dr. Laura Slack evaluates gut health, systemic inflammation, nutritional deficiencies, and hormone levels.</p>\n<p>Combining targeted IV Therapy, bioidentical hormone balancing, or peptide support ensures your body has the internal groundwork required for lasting clear skin.</p>\n<h2>Why Local Patients Trust Dr. Laura Slack &amp; Imber Medical</h2>\n<p>Choosing the right provider for severe acne makes all the difference in achieving clear skin without damaging your skin barrier.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Physician-Led Care:</strong> Dr. Laura Slack holds board certifications in family and geriatric medicine, alongside clinical certifications in aesthetic and anti-aging medicine from the American Academy of Procedural Medicine (AAPM).</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Tailored Treatment Plans:</strong> We carefully evaluate your skin type, medical history, and lifestyle to design a personalized regimen rather than pushing generic protocols.</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Cutting-Edge Innovation:</strong> Located right on Frederica Road, our practice brings top-tier aesthetic technologies and functional wellness directly to the St. Simons Island and greater Brunswick communities.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Take the First Step Toward Clear Skin Today</h2>\n<p>You do not have to live with painful breakouts or guess which products might work. If you are struggling with a severe flare-up, visit the expert team at Imber Medical for a customized clinical skin assessment.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Address:</strong> 1620 Frederica Road, St. Simons Island, GA 31522</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Phone:</strong> 912-268-2103</li>\n\n\n\n<li><strong>Hours:</strong> Monday – Friday: 9:00 AM – 5:00 PM</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Call 912-268-2103 today or schedule your consultation online to explore your options for severe acne flare-up treatments on St. Simons Island!</strong></p>"
